# gamedev.mdc

These rules apply to Cam’s video game dev in this workspace.
Goal is fun, tiny, and easy to understand.

## Keep it simple

- Start with simple HTML5 + JavaScript games.
- Prefer a single `index.html` that just works.
- No complicated engines. No heavy setups.
- Touch-friendly controls (big buttons).

## Phone-first game feel

- Big text and big tap targets.
- Clear “Start”, “Pause”, “Reset” buttons.
- Fast loading. Works offline if possible.

## Readable code

- Keep files short.
- Use clear names like `score`, `timer`, `level`.
- Don’t overbuild. Make it playable first.

## Folder shape

- One game = one folder:
  - `games/<game-name>/index.html`

